WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.000
The Rabbanites, the people who believe in Judaism and practice Judaism, the way we practice it ourselves, were only a minority.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:24.000
It's very important to remember. The, I mean, if we want to call it an orthodox world at the time, was a minority to the Karahites.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:33.000
In addition to this, the second immediately says, sorry, Rabban says, he has to pay me.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:44.000
So, Judaism, and this is a Jewish community, for the first time had access to the law.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:58.000
What does this mean? It meant the following revolution. That the community, the lay people, were in charge of directing the affairs of the Karahites.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Not the Rabbis, not the clergy, before it was the clergy. Only the clergy had access to the Tora.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:13.000
And therefore, the coming people, or the lay people, or the community, or the parnasim, had no access.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.000
So the first year comes the first revolution, Mishne Tora.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Through the Mishne Tora, all of a sudden the people, the coming people, could organize themselves and could supervise the Rabbis.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Another thing, which is very, very important, the commentary to the Mishneh.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Somebody tells you the Talmud is this and that, a person with a little bit of knowledge, knowledge of Arabic also, because that was the common language,

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.000
he could open and he could have access to the Talmudic lore.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Now, the two things. Community, for the first time now the community, the power is in the hands of the community.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.000
And we have a book, and the term is called Tora Control.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Besides this, Ramban, with his own personality, changed the habits of the community.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Let me give you one example from Halab.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:25.000
There is a question, that the community in Halab, they ask him, are we permitted to listen to the songs of the goyim?

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:31.000
They love Arabic music. Are we permitted to go and listen to Arabic music?

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.000
Ramban, will you agree with him or not?

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.000
He believed, no.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Listen to this, interestingly.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.000
He says, no, you should not listen.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:49.000
If you want to listen, then you have to write your own words in Hebrew.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:55.000
This is the beginning of the institution that we call Pakashot.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:04.000
The whole notion of Pakashot, of Pizmorim, that you take Arabic music and you put Arabic music into Hebrew words.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:11.000
That was a direct effect of Ramban's position.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.000
Now, here comes one more point, and then we are going to see what happened.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:26.000
In the East, in the Middle East, Jews were in commerce.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.000
They were actually in international commerce.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:35.000
The whole Mediterranean and all commerce with India was in the hands of the Jews in the Middle East.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Now, Ramban, not only that he promoted this type of leadership, but here comes something interesting.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:52.000
For the first time, it is the businessmen who become the people of power in the Jewish community.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:04:00.000
He is not a physician, he is not a scientist, he is not a scholar, he is a man of action.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:07.000
A final note, Ramban, believe it or not, never occupied a rabbinic position in his life.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.000
You know what he was?

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:13.000
He was the president of the community, not the Ribbi of the community.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:20.000
And we come here and it changes the whole role of the lay community, the lay people,

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:26.000
and above all, the possibility of the president who is the one who is acting.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:35.000
Now, when Ramban left Spain as a child, probably at the age of 12, 15, Spain was the paradise.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:43.000
Jews had wealth, it was the only country in which there was absolutely no anti-Semitism.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:49.000
Jews were in power and it was a kind of paradise.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:57.000
